# Age of War season — do not push to main

The **Royal Armies Age of War** seasonal event is **in development**. Do **not** commit or push seasonal work to `main` until the user explicitly says the season is ready to ship (e.g. "ship Age of War", "push the season", "release seasonal content").

Pushing `main` deploys production ([royalarmies.com](https://royalarmies.com)).

## Seasonal scope (hold all of this)

- **Black game page** / opening cinematic shell on `game.html`
- **Opening prologue** — narration, subtitles, cue timing, distressed-woman audio
- **End-of-narration logos** — title/subtitle fly-in, lore tool, Enter the War gate
- **Music transitions** — main → game → age handoff, Archimedes / Kindred / Cascading Skies sequencing, hidden vs visible player states
- **Age page Age of War branding** — `royalarmiessubtitlelogo.png`, right-HUD subtitle slot, vertical centering/nudges, spark bursts on that logo
- **Bottom-bar music player** placement tied to the age soundtrack flow (when part of season audio UX)
- **Any future files or edits** clearly for this seasonal event (prologue, season HUD, season audio, season copy)

## Canonical seasonal paths

Treat these as **season-only** unless the user says otherwise:

| Path | Notes |
|------|--------|
| `public/rift-opening-prologue.js` | Prologue runtime |
| `public/rift-subtitle-logo-sparks.js` | Subtitle/logo sparks (prologue + age HUD logo) |
| `public/age-music-flow.js` | Cross-page soundtrack flow |
| `public/images/royalarmiessubtitlelogo.png` | Age of War subtitle asset |
| `public/audio/distressedwoman.mp3` | Opening narration |
| `public/game.html`, `public/game.js` | Prologue/cinematic/black-screen hooks (often mixed) |
| `public/agealpha.html`, `public/age-page.js` | Age HUD subtitle + related script/CSS busts |
| `public/style2.css` | Blocks: `.game-opening-prologue*`, `.age-map-hud-subtitle*`, `.age-bottom-music*`, prologue lore/enter-war |
| `public/main.html`, `public/script2.js` | Main-page music suppression / handoff (when seasonal) |

**Mixed files** (`game.html`, `style2.css`, `script2.js`, `mobile-responsive.css`, etc.) may contain both seasonal and non-seasonal edits. Do **not** push the whole file to `main` if the diff includes seasonal hunks—split work or keep changes on the season branch only.

## Not seasonal (OK to push to main)

- Bug fixes, NEXUS/API, guild/city/gameplay systems, mail, portal metrics, rank reset, cursor/modal z-index, dev-environment/Live Server fixes
- **Global UI SFX** (`public/rift-ui-sfx.js`) when not prologue-specific—unless the change only serves the opening cinematic

When unsure, ask or keep the change on the season branch.

## Git workflow

1. **Save seasonal work** on branch `season/age-of-war` (create from current season tip if needed).
2. **Do not push** seasonal commits to `origin/main`.
3. For tasks that touch both seasonal and non-seasonal code:
   - Commit/push **only non-seasonal** paths to `main`, or
   - Finish on `season/age-of-war` and tell the user seasonal files were held back.
4. Overrides `auto-commit-deploy` for seasonal paths: **commit locally or on the season branch is fine; no push to `main`.**

## Releasing later

When the user approves release: merge or cherry-pick `season/age-of-war` → `main`, bump all related `?v=` cache busts, then push once.
